  "description": "JISYET crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H58 Eu1 N8 O36 Si8 Tb1 Y2 2-,2(C8 H20 N1 1+). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Y2? (Y) has 0 O neighbors; Y1? (Y) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.703-3.718 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.46-106.93°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [NEt4]2[(Ph4Si4O8)2Eu0.87Tb1.01Y2.11(NO3)6(EtOH)2(MeCN)2]·2EtOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
